WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.680
In male CBA/CaJ mice, after loud noise, hearing thresholds can come back to normal.

2
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.840
Yet the cochlea has lost about half of its ribbon synapses at one place.

3
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.040
How can the test miss that?

4
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.440
A threshold is only the quietest sound that gets a response.

5
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.960
It says little about how many synapses carry the rest.

6
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:28.893
Start with the inner hair cell.

7
00:00:29.493 --> 00:00:34.893
It releases transmitter continuously onto auditory nerve fibres, at ribbon synapses.

8
00:00:35.693 --> 00:00:38.393
The ribbon is a dense structure at the release site.

9
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.453
In mouse, it keeps a larger pool of vesicles in supply.

10
00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:45.533
A threshold does not count these synapses.

11
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:51.877
Kujawa and Liberman tested this in male CBA/CaJ mice.

12
00:00:52.657 --> 00:00:59.477
They played noise at 8 to 16 kHz, at 100 dB SPL, for two hours.

13
00:01:00.237 --> 00:01:05.017
By two weeks, thresholds were back to their old values, and the hair cells were

14
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:11.877
intact. But at eight weeks, the ribbon count at the 32 kHz place was about 50%

15
00:01:11.877 --> 00:01:15.097
below control. The nerve degenerated later.

16
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.790
In people, no living synapse count exists.

17
00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.210
So two studies used proxies.

18
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:29.190
In 34 young adults, the higher-risk group had a higher SP to AP ratio.

19
00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:33.550
The authors called it consistent with selective neural loss.

20
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:38.470
But that group also had raised thresholds at 10 to 16 kHz.

21
00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:45.770
A second study compared 16 listeners with trouble hearing speech in noise against 16

22
00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.830
matched controls. It found no association.

23
00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:53.190
The authors allowed that the measures might not be sensitive enough.

24
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.020
The same care applies to treatment numbers.

25
00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:04.600
In one child in an early OTOF gene therapy trial, the baseline ABR threshold was

26
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.240
above the 95 decibel test ceiling in each ear.

27
00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:15.960
At week 26 it was 58 decibels, so the improvement was more than 37 decibels.

28
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.620
That is a lower bound, not an exact value.

29
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.520
And it is not a percentage of hearing restored.

30
00:02:23.483 --> 00:02:29.543
A complaint, a proposed lesion and a validated test are three different things.

31
00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:34.503
A normal threshold did not mean intact synapses in these mice.

32
00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:37.603
A proxy is not a synapse count.

33
00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:42.643
A value past the ceiling gives a bound, not an exact change.

34
00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:46.623
So ask what a number counts, and what it leaves out.
